# Build output. Everything the build produces lives under artifacts/ and none of it is committed.
/artifacts/

# Per-project intermediates, for anything that escapes the artifacts pivot.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# COMPILED CONTENT IS A BUILD OUTPUT.
#
# assets/ holds what a human edits - the .fx shader sources, and in time the .png, .wav and
# .spritefont. The .xnb the pipeline produces from them does not belong in git: it would make
# every texture tweak a binary diff, and it is reproducible from what is here.
#
# The game's own art, audio and models are not here at all and never will be - they are not part
# of what Refactored Games released, and you need your own copy of the game. See license.md.
/Content/
*.xnb

# The shader compiler: a pinned clone of our ShadowDusk fork plus natives from NuGet, assembled
# by tools/shadowdusk/build-shadowdusk.sh into artifacts/. Fetched, never vendored - 155 MB
# across all RIDs, and a 27 MB .so never delta-compresses, so committing it would add a full
# copy to history on every rebuild.
/tools/shadowdusk/bin/

# Player state, if someone runs the game from the tree.
/user/
/Saves/
Options.xml
ModSettings.xml

# Runtime droppings. A stale Errors.txt shipped in every package for weeks once, looking like a
# report on the build you had just made.
Errors.txt
RenderTrace.txt
/RenderTrace/

# Editors and OS
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
